The backend was functionally complete but the repository root had no entry
point: a new teammate landed on a bare `repo/` folder with no overview and no
statement of what is finished. This commit finishes the deliverable.

* `repo/README.md` – project overview: the game idea, per-layer status, a
  three-command quickstart, the real file map, the 8-stage / 15-mission campaign
  table, controls → endpoints, continuity, scientific honesty, and the frontend
  hand-off.
* `repo/PROJECT_STATUS.md` – Arabic status report built from commands that were
  actually executed: gate results, campaign scores, live NASA probes, known
  limits and the next phase.
* `tests/test_project_docs.py` (8 tests) – docs get a gate like everything else:
  the campaign tables must match `content/missions/`, local links must resolve,
  and the status report must quote the published contract.
* `docs/verification-2026-11-12.md` – dated record of the full run (dependency
  versions, gate output, campaign table, live-integration probes).
* `reference/scratch/` – drop the two reproducible 290 KB payload dumps, keep
  `capture.py` and document how to regenerate them; ignore future dumps.
* refresh the quoted test count (429 → 437) everywhere.

Verified on Python 3.11 / FastAPI 0.162.5: ruff, ruff format, mypy, content
validation, route audit and the OpenAPI contract check are clean; 437 tests pass
with 93% coverage; the campaign plays 15/15 missions (93 actions, 0 mistakes)
through public HTTP; NASA POWER and APOD both answered `provenance: live`.
